  "notes": "West leads the ♠K against 6♥. The defense starts with 2 rounds of spades, South ruffing the second round. It looks like South has no more losers, but the blockage in diamonds may cause trouble if hearts are 4-1 and diamonds are 5-1.\n\nSouth should begin by drawing 2 rounds of trump. The 4-1 break means that South cannot draw all of the remaining trumps. The South hand would also be out of trumps and South's diamonds would be stranded.\n\nSouth should not try to cash both of dummy's diamonds before drawing the remaining trumps. The defender with 4 hearts may also have a singleton diamond and will be able to score a ruff.\n\nSouth should cash only 1 round of diamonds before drawing the remaining trumps. On the last round of trump North's remaining diamond honour is discarded, unblocking the suit. South is free to cash his diamonds and easily take the rest of the tricks.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♠K against 6♥. The defense starts with 2 rounds of spades, South ruffing the second round. It looks like South has no more losers, but the blockage in diamonds may cause trouble if hearts are 4-1 and diamonds are 5-1.",
    "South should begin by drawing 2 rounds of trump. The 4-1 break means that South cannot draw all of the remaining trumps. The South hand would also be out of trumps and South's diamonds would be stranded.",
    "South should not try to cash both of dummy's diamonds before drawing the remaining trumps. The defender with 4 hearts may also have a singleton diamond and will be able to score a ruff.",
    "South should cash only 1 round of diamonds before drawing the remaining trumps. On the last round of trump North's remaining diamond honour is discarded, unblocking the suit. South is free to cash his diamonds and easily take the rest of the tricks."
